NAME

ulibCatDeleteFile - Deletes an entry from the file catalogue


SYNOPSIS

UBYTE ulibCatDeleteFile(struct CatCommand *Cmd)
                                 a0


DESCRIPTION

This function deletes an entry from the file catalogue.

Only the following elements of the CatCommand structure are used:

   <File1>
        File1->Name is the name of the entry to delete.

   <Flags>
        PhysicalFileAlso - If this bit is set, the physical file will also
                           be deleted if the catalogue deletion is successful.

Note, this function currently does not take notice of the RetainHandles flag.


RETURNS

0        - Success
Non-zero - Failure

              1 - Failure to delete first key
              2 - Couldn't find physical file
              3 - Couldn't delete physical file
              4 - Failure to delete second key
